Whole plant foods provide vitamins C, E, K, folate, potassium, and magnesium at levels that animal-dominant diets typically cannot match.
The Academy of Nutrition and Dietetics states that well-planned vegan diets are nutritionally adequate for all stages of life, from infancy through old age.
Legumes — beans, lentils, chickpeas — provide complete protein profiles when combined across a day, at a fraction of the cost and environmental impact of animal protein.
